ASR system, with the audio signal remaining barely distinguishable from the original signal. In an experimental evaluation, we attack the state-of-the-art speech recognition system Kaldi and determine the best performing parameter and analysis setup for different types of input. Our results show that we are successful in up to 98% of cases with a computational effort of fewer than two minutes for a ten-second audio file. Based on user studies, we found that none of our target transcriptions were audible to human listeners, who still understand the original speech content with unchanged accuracy.\n\nSubjects:\n\nCryptography and Security (cs.CR); Sound (cs.SD); Audio and Speech Processing (eess.AS)\n\nCite as:\n\n[arXiv:1808.05665](https://arxiv.org/abs/1808.05665) \\[cs.CR\\]\n\n \n\n(or [arXiv:1808.05665v2](https://arxiv.org/abs/1808.05665v2) \\[cs.CR\\] for this version)\n\n \n\n[https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.1808.05665](https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.1808.05665)\n\nFocus to learn more\n\narXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\n\nSubmission history\n------------------\n\nFrom: Lea Schönherr \\[[view email](/show-email/2c82b5c3/1808.05665)\\]  \n**[\\[v1\\]](/abs/1808.05665v1)** Thu, 16 Aug 2018 20:00:47 UTC (1,401 KB)  \n**\\[v2\\]** Tue, 30 Oct 2018 12:02:07 UTC (1,033 KB)  \n\nFull-text links:\n\nAccess Paper:\n-------------\n\nView a PDF of the paper titled Adversarial Attacks Against Automatic Speech Recognition Systems via Psychoacoustic Hiding, by Lea Sch\\\\\"onherr and 4 other authors\n\n*   [View PDF](/pdf/1808.05665)\n*   [HTML (experimental)](https://arxiv.org/html/1808.05665v2)\n*   [TeX Source](/src/1808.05665)\n\n[view license](http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/ \"Rights to this article\")\n\n### Additional Features\n\n*   [Audio Summary](/audio/1808.05665)\n\n### Current browse context:\n\ncs.CR\n\n[< prev](/prevnext?id=1808.05665&function=prev&context=cs.CR \"previous in cs.CR (accesskey p)\")   |   [next >](/prevnext?id=1808.05665&functio